Privacy Controls and DPIA for Regulated Workloads
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Set up a local privacy assessment workbook using open-source tools
Classify PII categories and determine lawful bases for processing under GDPR/PDPL
Execute a DPIA workflow and document residual privacy risks
Map mitigations to NIST SP 800-53 PT (Privacy) and PM (Program Management) control families
Generate and digitally sign a DPIA report
Prerequisites
Basic Linux command-line familiarity (file navigation, text editors)
Understanding of GDPR/PDPL fundamentals and NIST SP 800-53 control structure
Familiarity with CGRC Domain 3 (Risk Response) and Domain 4 (Controls) concepts
No prior scripting expertise required, but comfort editing YAML/Markdown is helpful
